greycroft-scopely:greenhouse:4981705008.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;Pikmin Bloom, a geo-location based mobile game developed by Niantic, launched globally in October 2021, and has been steadily growing its user base - it now has millions of users worldwide. For wandering and spending time outside, users are rewarded with items that can either grow or feed the curious creatures called Pikmin introduced in the console game by Nintendo. Pikmin Bloom is the largest mobile game for the Pikmin IP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Niantic is looking for a Marketing Director to lead the overall marketing strategy, go-to-market execution, and long-term business growth for Pikmin Bloom across North America. This role will serve as the senior regional marketing leader, overseeing integrated marketing initiatives across user acquisition, engagement, retention, partnerships, social/community, and live experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a strategic and highly collaborative leader with deep expertise in mobile game marketing, a strong understanding of the live-service gaming business, and a passion for building impactful player experiences. This individual will lead and develop a high-performing team while partnering closely with executive stakeholders, cross-functional teams, and external partners across both North America and Japan.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As this is a global product, you will collaborate extensively with international teammates to ensure alignment, consistency, and operational excellence across all regions and major marketing initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the North America marketing vision, strategy, and execution for Pikmin Bloom, driving sustainable growth across player acquisition, engagement, retention, and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and develop a high-performing regional marketing organization across multiple workstreams, including user acquisition, social/community marketing, partnerships, live events, and campaign execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate product and business objectives into integrated operational marketing plans with measurable impact across the North America region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product positioning, key messaging, and audience strategies informed by player insights, market dynamics, and competitive analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead go-to-market planning and execution for major product initiatives, seasonal campaigns, feature launches, partnerships, and real-world activations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product Management, Game Design, Engineering, Business Development, Operations, Communications, Legal, Analytics, and executive leadership to align marketing strategy with broader business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive alignment and effective collaboration between North America and Japan-based stakeholders across global marketing initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and manage the regional marketing budget, including resource allocation, forecasting, ROI analysis, and optimization against business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish performance goals and KPIs across marketing initiatives, including awareness, acquisition, DAU, WAU, retention, engagement, ARPU, and revenue contribution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use data, experimentation, and market insights to evaluate campaign effectiveness and continuously optimize strategies and investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with external agencies, platform partners, media partners, and IP stakeholders to maximize marketing impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead organizational planning, recruiting, coaching, and talent development for the marketing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a collaborative, inclusive, and high-accountability culture that enables teams to execute effectively in a fast-paced global environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate organizational and operational risks proactively and implement scalable processes to support long-term growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Encourage the use of AI tools and automation to improve marketing workflows, campaign effectiveness, and team efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore practical applications of emerging AI capabilities across areas such as creative development, audience insights, reporting, and campaign optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12+ years of experience in marketing, gaming, entertainment, or consumer technology industries, including significant experience in mobile/live-service gaming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading integrated marketing strategy and execution for large-scale consumer products or live-service games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing and developing high-performing marketing teams, including managers and senior individual contributors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in product positioning, go-to-market strategy, user acquisition, engagement, retention, and lifecycle marketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience overseeing paid media strategy and execution, including creative development, agency management, media planning/buying, campaign optimization, and performance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading highly cross-functional initiatives involving multiple internal teams, external partners, and executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen with the ability to balance strategic priorities, operational execution, and financial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing substantial marketing budgets and evaluating ROI against business objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding verbal and written communication skills, including experience presenting to executive leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with the ability to leverage data and consumer insights to inform decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced hybrid environment with evolving priorities and ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for creating meaningful player experiences that connect digital and real-world engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-powered marketing tools and emerging AI trends relevant to consumer marketing and live-service games.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in applying AI and automation to improve marketing workflows, creativity, and operational efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;For candidates in CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA, the annual salary range is provided below. In addition to base pay, employees may be eligible for equity, bonuses, and a comprehensive benefits package, including healthcare benefits, retirement benefits, pet insurance, paid holidays, paid Scopely free days, and unlimited paid time off. Base pay offered may vary depending on job-related knowledge, skills, and experience.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;CA, CO, NJ, NY, and WA Annual Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$161,500&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$238,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About Scopely&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is a leading video game and global interactive entertainment company, home to many of the world’s most beloved and enduring experiences, including two of the most successful mobile games of all-time “MONOPOLY GO!” and “Pokémon GO,” along with “Stumble Guys,” “Star Trek™ Fleet Command,” “MARVEL Strike Force,” “WWE Champions,” the Scrabble® franchise, “Yahtzee® With Buddies,” and many others. Across mobile, web, PC, and console, Scopely creates, develops, publishes, and live-operates one of the most diversified and award-winning portfolios in the games industry — bringing hundreds of millions of players together through a shared love of play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, Scopely is powered by its exceptional team — including thousands of world-class gamemakers around the globe, a distinctive tenet-driven culture, and its proprietary technology platform, Playgami. Together, these strengths have fueled Scopely’s position as the #1 mobile games company in the U.S. and #2 globally, generating more than $10 billion in lifetime revenue. Whether building global sensations like “MONOPOLY GO!” from the ground up, or expanding through strategic acquisitions, including the FoxNext, GSN, and Niantic games businesses — Scopely consistently delivers experiences players love today and return to for years to come.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Recognized multiple times as one of the &quot;100 Most Influential Companies in the World&quot; by TIME magazine and one of Fast Company&#39;s &quot;World&#39;s Most Innovative Companies&quot; and “Best Workplaces for Innovators,” Scopely believes that video games can be a force for good — creating meaningful connections, vibrant communities, and making life better through play.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Scopely has global operations and partners across four continents in more than a dozen countries worldwide. For more information, visit: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/&quot;&gt;https://www.scopely.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notice to Candidates: Scopely will never request payment or financial information during the application or hiring process. Please apply only through our official &lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;website&lt;/a&gt; and verify that all Talent Partner communications come from an email address ending in @&lt;a href=&quot;http://scopely.com&quot;&gt;scopely.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions or encounter any fraudulent requests/emails/websites, please immediately contact recruiting@scopely.com. Our job applicant privacy policies are available here: &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/job-applicant-privacy-notice-for-ca-residents&quot;&gt;California Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.scopely.com/en/eea-and-uk-job-applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;EEA/UK Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Employment at Scopely is based solely on a person&#39;s merit and qualifications. Scopely does not discriminate against any employee or applicant because of race, creed, color, religion, gender, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, national origin, disability, age, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding), or any other basis protected by law. We also consider qualified applicants with arrest or conviction records, consistent with applicable federal, state and local law.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

greycroft-scopely:greenhouse:5121922008.descriptionHtml:
&lt;p&gt;Scopely is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Talent Coordinator&lt;/strong&gt; to join our Talent Acquisition team operating on a hybrid schedule from our Bangalore hub! This hybrid role involves working from the office 3–5 days per week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Scopely, we care deeply about what we do and want to inspire play, every day - whether in our work environments alongside our talented colleagues, or through our deep connections with our communities of players. We are a global team of game lovers who are developing, publishing and innovating the mobile games industry, connecting millions of people around the world daily.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We make sure our teams have everything they need to create amazing games. The People team manages everything from benefits &amp;amp; employee engagement to professional development opportunities and more!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Talent Coordinator, you’re not just managing logistics, you’re orchestrating a candidate experience that reflects who we are and what we value. You are the engine behind our recruiting process that empowers interviewers to show up prepared, talent partners to focus on strategy, and candidates to bring their best selves. You thrive at getting things done in a fast-moving and ever-evolving environment and you&#39;re not afraid to take smart risks to make things better.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate and arrange all candidate interviews, including booking travel accommodations for non-local candidates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage candidates in Greenhouse (applicant tracking system)&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion an exceptional candidate experience from start to finish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate complex interview schedules across global time zones with multiple participants&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Talent Partners (recruiters) to ensure a great candidate experience and facilitate processes such as interviews, offers, and background checks&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with People Operations, People Business Partners, and People Experience teams on efforts to optimize processes, workflow, and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist the Talent Acquisition team in tracking metrics, candidate surveys and reporting&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to the evolution of our recruitment processes by working closely with the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-volume recruitment coordination experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-directed, detail-oriented, problem solver with a burning desire to contribute&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop strong trusting relationships in a demanding and high-performing work environment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration, written and verbal communication skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gmail, Google Calendar and Google docs proficiency&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with an Applicant Tracking system or CRM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong English language skills are required for this role as we have a highly diverse and global business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
